id: pm-7i97c3
title: Every core and first-party package command declares an attributable agent intent
description: "summarizeCommandIntent (src/sdk/cli-contracts/runtime-contracts.ts:2429) resolves the exact command, then the root command, then returns the literal 'Inspect flags.' with no diagnostic and no payload marker, and COMMAND_INTENTS (:594) is a hand-maintained Map that nothing joins against the command catalog. Measured at HEAD on 2026.8.1: 32 of 76 canonical commands in pm contracts --summary carry the placeholder, including the core nouns merge, normalize, events, item, update-many, eval, search-advanced, close-many, test-all, test-runs, dedupe-audit, dedupe-merge and comments-audit. The summary is the first call of the documented two-call cold start (pm-ka6d) and costs 2,425 tokens against 54,718 for the full per-command help surface; recovering one missing intent via pm <command> --help costs roughly 580 tokens, so two recoveries exceed the summary's own price. Duplicate check: searched intent/summary/help-tier/one-line lineages and read pm-e2bq, pm-kxci8x, pm-ka6d, pm-wt43zj, pm-5t33or; none owns intent coverage as a contract."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:contracts",simplification
created_at: "2026-08-01T09:46:45.146Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-13T18:51:00.369Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-13T18:50:59.261Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-13T18:50:59.261Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "Every command in the catalog resolves to a declared intent by construction with no fallback string; package-contributed commands declare intent through the contribution manifest; intent shape is constrained (imperative, names the noun and read/write direction, within a declared character budget, unique across commands); coverage and uniqueness are machine-checked in the noun-verb conformance pass so a command without an intent cannot merge"
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Make the machine-readable command summary answer what each command is for, for every command"
value: The 91 percent token saving the summary offers stops being conditional on which command an agent needs
why_now: The gap reached 42 percent silently because no state of the repository makes it visible except by counting; each new command widens it
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: Replaced placeholder intents with explicit core and first-party package intent contracts.
expected_result: "Every catalog command resolves a constrained, attributable intent without a placeholder."
actual_result: Core paths and ten first-party packages declare intents; conformance refuses placeholders and tests provenance.
