comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T11:15:43.989Z","harness:codex","Live contract delta 2026-08-03: 31 of 76 canonical summary commands still emit the placeholder intent Inspect flags. The historical title records 32 at discovery time; current evidence shows one improvement but 40.8 percent of the canonical cold-start surface remains non-explanatory. Keep the item open until the machine check reaches zero and prevents recurrence."
  "2026-08-04T09:18:08.582Z","harness:codex","Fresh contract census 2026-08-04 remains 76 canonical command summaries, 31 placeholder intents reading Inspect flags., 21 commands without a default token budget, and 111 advertised flag mentions. The placeholder count is unchanged from 2026-08-03 and still leaves 40.8 percent of the designated cold-start command surface semantically unexplained."
  "2026-08-13T14:30:33.429Z","harness:claude-code","Re-measured 2026-08-13 with a wider denominator, which changes the size of the problem rather than confirming it.\n\nCounting top-level commands, the placeholder census is now 29 of 72 rather than 32 of 76, so the ratio is roughly unchanged while the surface shrank by four.\n\nCounting declared command paths — the unit an agent actually resolves — the picture is different. contracts --json --full declares 159 paths: 81 top-level and 78 subcommand. It emits 72 summaries, six of which name extension command groups that appear in no path list, so 66 declared paths carry a summary and 93 carry none. Every subcommand path is in the uncovered set. Combining both effects, a path that states a real intent exists for 43 of 159, or 27 percent.\n\nThe consequence for this item's scope: closing it by filling in 29 placeholder strings would leave 93 paths with no row to hold an intent at all. Filed pm-pmrae8 for the coverage half, which also carries the sequencing risk that every consolidation under pm-n7rr moves a command from the covered half into the uncovered one."
  "2026-08-13T15:27:26.854Z","harness:codex","TDD red evidence: summary construction still emits generic 'Inspect flags.' and collapses namespaced/aliased paths; new regression coverage rejects the placeholder and requires deterministic exact-path intent."
  "2026-08-13T17:12:51.002Z","harness:codex","Completion evidence: all active core command paths have explicit operation-derived intents, all ten first-party contribution packages declare manifest intent, package intent takes precedence with disclosed description/path fallback for third-party compatibility, and placeholder intent is refused by contract tests. Linked contracts test passed 48/48; exact full suite passed 7,262 tests at 100/100/100/100; static/docstring/security gates passed."
  "2026-08-13T18:11:51.375Z","harness:codex","PR #999 TDD red: generated intents remained singular for extension/package adopt-all and workspace snapshot list; disabling aliases emitted the opposite finite-limit hint, and health/validate still advertised unregistered --verbose. Focused review suite: 92 passed, 4 failed as expected."
  "2026-08-13T18:50:47.353Z","harness:codex","PR #999 review-resolution evidence: disabling legacy truncation aliases now instructs --output-limit unbounded, and health/validate no longer advertise an unregistered --verbose flag. Focused read-output regressions passed; the full exact suite validates catalog parity."
